3. Functional & Technical Requirements
3.1 Natural Language Query (NLQ)
Objective

Allow users to type analytical questions in natural language and receive visual answers.

Functional Requirements

User can type queries like:

"Show total revenue by region."

"Top 5 products by profit."

"Sales trend for 2025."

"Compare revenue and cost by month."

System must:

Parse intent.

Identify:

Measures

Dimensions

Time context

Aggregation type

Generate:

Query plan

Recommended chart

Render result instantly.

Allow manual refinement.

NLQ Processing Pipeline

Text preprocessing.

Schema matching (map words to fields).

Intent detection (aggregation, comparison, trend).

Query plan generation.

Chart selection logic.

Execution via query engine.

Example Output Structure
{
  "parsedQuery": {
    "measure": "SUM(Revenue)",
    "dimension": "Region",
    "chartType": "bar"
  }
}
Acceptance Criteria

Recognizes dataset fields correctly.

Correct aggregation applied.

Correct chart suggested.

Ambiguous queries prompt clarification.

Works within 1–2 seconds typical case.

3.2 AI Insight Generation
Objective

Automatically surface meaningful insights from dataset.

Functional Requirements

System must analyze dataset and detect:

Highest/lowest values.

Strong trends.

Significant percentage changes.

Top contributing categories.

Distribution skewness.

Insights must:

Update when filters change.

Be optionally auto-generated.

Be dismissible by user.

Insight Structure
{
  "insights": [
    {
      "type": "trend",
      "message": "Revenue increased 24% compared to last month."
    }
  ]
}
Acceptance Criteria

Insight accurate.

Reflects active filters.

Updates dynamically.

No misleading conclusions.

3.3 Anomaly Detection System
Objective

Detect unusual patterns in time-series or numeric distributions.

Functional Requirements

System must detect:

Sudden spikes

Sudden drops

Outliers

Statistical deviations (e.g., > 2 standard deviations)

Applicable to:

Line charts

Time-series measures

Scatter plots

Detected anomalies must:

Be visually highlighted.

Show explanation tooltip.

Configuration Example
{
  "anomalyDetection": {
    "enabled": true,
    "sensitivity": "medium"
  }
}
Acceptance Criteria

Outliers highlighted correctly.

Works with filters.

False positives minimized.

Performance acceptable.

3.4 Smart Narrative Generator
Objective

Generate human-readable summaries of dashboards.

Functional Requirements

System must generate summary text like:

"Revenue reached its highest value in Q4 2025."

"East region contributed 42% of total revenue."

"Sales show a steady upward trend."

Narratives must:

Reflect current filters.

Update automatically.

Be editable by user.

Be exportable.

Narrative Structure
{
  "narrative": "Revenue increased steadily over the past 6 months, with Q4 being the strongest quarter."
}
Acceptance Criteria

Text matches actual data.

No contradictions.

Updates when filters change.

Export includes narrative.

3.5 AI-Powered Chart Recommendation (Advanced)
Objective

Move from rule-based to intelligent chart selection.

Functional Requirements

System must evaluate:

Data distribution

Cardinality

Variance

Correlation

Historical user behavior

Use ML model or heuristics to recommend:

Optimal chart

Optimal aggregation

Potential drill hierarchy

Recommendations must:

Appear during chart creation.

Rank suggestions.

Allow override.

Recommendation Output
{
  "recommendations": [
    { "chart": "line", "confidence": 0.87 },
    { "chart": "area", "confidence": 0.65 }
  ]
}
Acceptance Criteria

Suggestions contextually accurate.

Confidence score logical.

Overrides allowed.

Learns from usage patterns (optional advanced).

3.6 Conversational Analytics Interface
Objective

Provide chat-style interaction for analytics.

Functional Requirements

User can:

Ask follow-up questions.

Refine previous query.

Request explanation of chart.

Ask "Why did revenue drop in March?"

System must:

Maintain conversation context.

Refer to active dashboard.

Clarify ambiguous questions.

Provide visual + textual output.

Context Structure
{
  "conversationContext": {
    "activeMeasure": "Revenue",
    "activeDimension": "Month",
    "filters": []
  }
}
Acceptance Criteria

Context maintained across messages.

Follow-up queries modify existing chart.

Clarification prompts work.

No incorrect schema references.

3.7 Model Monitoring & Explainability
Objective

Ensure AI transparency and reliability.

Requirements

System must:

Log AI decisions.

Provide explanation for:

Why chart chosen.

Why anomaly detected.

Allow users to disable AI features.

Provide confidence scores.

Acceptance Criteria

AI decisions explainable.

Confidence shown.

Users can disable AI modules.

Logs available for debugging.

